10 REM MINIBNCH -- TEN PASSES OF A THOUSAND ADDS, TIMED
20 REM
30 REM THE PROGRAM IS LINES 200-270, THE WAY IT WAS TYPED
40 REM AT THE MACHINE. EVERYTHING ELSE IS THE CLOCK ROUND
50 REM IT, AND THE MARKER DOTS STAY INSIDE THE MEASUREMENT
60 REM BECAUSE THEY ARE PART OF THE PROGRAM BEING TIMED.
70 REM
80 REM TIMER IS THE VBLANK COUNT, 59.97 A SECOND: A TICK
90 REM IS 16.7 MS, SIX TIMES FINER THAN A TENTH. IT WRAPS
100 REM AT 65536 FRAMES AND THE SUBTRACTION WRAPS WITH IT,
110 REM SO ONLY A RUN PAST NINE MINUTES WOULD NEED MORE.
120 MODE 0
130 CURSOR 0
135 CLS
140 PRINT "MINIBNCH -- 10 PASSES OF 1000 ADDS"
150 PRINT
170 T=TIMER
200 FOR I=1 TO 10
210 S=0
220 FOR J=1 TO 1000
230 S=S+J
240 NEXT J
250 PRINT ".";
260 NEXT I
270 PRINT S
280 F=TIMER-T
290 E#=F/59.97
300 PRINT
310 PRINT "TIME  ";E#;" S IN ";F;" FRAMES"
320 PRINT "PASS  ";E#/10;" S EACH, 1000 ADDS A PASS"
325 PRINT "SUM   ";S;" -- 500500 WRAPPED TO 16 BITS"
330 REM
340 REM S IS AN INTEGER, SO 500500 COMES BACK AS -23788:
350 REM THE SUM IS RIGHT AND THE WORD IS SIXTEEN BITS.
360 REM S# WOULD HOLD IT BUT ONLY TO ABOUT FIVE DIGITS,
370 REM AND IT WOULD BE FIVE TIMES SLOWER TO GET THERE.
380 END
